WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:17.066
could hardly believe his eyes.

2
00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:26.132
His former partner, Jacob Marley, stood there looking like a ghost, metal chains wrapped all around his transparent

3
00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:30.455
body. "What do you want from me, Marley?"

4
00:00:30.835 --> 00:00:31.616
Scrooge cried.

5
00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.210
"I want many things from you."

6
00:00:35.971 --> 00:00:38.333
Marley's voice sounded exactly the same.

7
00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:42.777
"In life, I was your partner, Jacob Marley."

8
00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:48.462
"Yes." Scrooge felt his legs wobble.

9
00:00:48.482 --> 00:00:51.825
"Can you sit down?"

10
00:00:51.845 --> 00:00:53.847
"I can."

11
00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:57.290
"Let's both do it, then."

12
00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:03.557
The two of them sat near the fire.

13
00:01:04.518 --> 00:01:07.320
Scrooge continued to stare at the ghost in disbelief.

14
00:01:08.661 --> 00:01:09.742
Marley cocked his head.

15
00:01:09.762 --> 00:01:13.904
"You don't believe in ghosts, Ebenezer, do you?"

16
00:01:15.386 --> 00:01:18.107
"Not normally," Scrooge said.

17
00:01:18.127 --> 00:01:24.812
"But tonight, so many strange things—" "Why do you doubt your senses?"

18
00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:26.553
Marley demanded.

19
00:01:26.573 --> 00:01:31.588
"Because little things can affect our senses," Scrooge said.

20
00:01:31.608 --> 00:01:40.011
"For example, you could be a hallucination caused by bad food I've eaten, like poorly cooked meat.

21
00:01:41.491 --> 00:01:46.213
Whatever you are, you do remind me more of gravy than a grave!"

22
00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:51.655
Scrooge rarely made jokes, for he had little sense of humor.

23
00:01:52.815 --> 00:01:56.056
But he was trying to keep down his terror in any way he could.

24
00:01:57.832 --> 00:02:01.415
The ghost of Jacob Marley was disturbing him to his bones.

25
00:02:02.896 --> 00:02:07.379
The figure moaned and shook his chains loudly, clearly not amused.

26
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.463
Scrooge held on tightly to his chair to prevent himself from fainting.

27
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:17.526
"Dreadful creature, why are you here?"

28
00:02:17.546 --> 00:02:21.468
"Do you believe in me or not?"

29
00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:22.869
Marley demanded.

30
00:02:25.331 --> 00:02:26.692
Scrooge closed his eyes.

31
00:02:28.692 --> 00:02:29.052
"I do.

32
00:02:29.492 --> 00:02:32.013
You are here so I must believe in you.

33
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:35.214
But why have you come to me?"

34
00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:43.817
"I wear these heavy chains, which I made myself, link by link and yard by yard.

35
00:02:45.057 --> 00:02:49.019
They are the result of the poor choices I made while alive."

36
00:02:50.159 --> 00:02:52.900
Marley glared at Scrooge with his awful eyes.

37
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.402
"You have made the same choices, Ebenezer.

38
00:02:59.523 --> 00:03:01.264
You continue to make them."

39
00:03:01.284 --> 00:03:04.866
"Jacob," Scrooge said.

40
00:03:04.886 --> 00:03:07.248
"This is terrifying.

41
00:03:08.248 --> 00:03:10.090
Say something that will comfort me."

42
00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:15.253
"I have no comfort to give," Marley said.

43
00:03:15.273 --> 00:03:19.836
"I am doomed to drag these chains with me as a ghost.

44
00:03:21.136 --> 00:03:26.200
It's my punishment for a lifetime of selfishness, pettiness, and greed."

45
00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.964
"But you were always so good at business," Scrooge said.

46
00:03:31.984 --> 00:03:36.027
"Business?" Marley scoffed.

47
00:03:36.047 --> 00:03:38.789
"Humans should have been my business!

48
00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.592
Charity, mercy, and kindness should have been my business.

49
00:03:46.134 --> 00:03:48.096
But, listen to me closely, Ebenezer.

50
00:03:49.236 --> 00:03:51.037
My time with you is short.

51
00:03:52.158 --> 00:03:57.381
And I'm here to warn you that you have only one chance of escaping the same fate.

52
00:03:58.281 --> 00:04:01.503
Tonight you will be haunted by three ghosts."

53
00:04:03.084 --> 00:04:04.025
Scrooge gulped.

54
00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:06.166
"More ghosts?

55
00:04:07.127 --> 00:04:09.368
I think I'd rather just go to bed!"

56
00:04:09.388 --> 00:04:16.212
"Without their visits, you are doomed to follow the same path that I walk.

57
00:04:17.544 --> 00:04:20.947
These ghosts will show you the way to save yourself.

58
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.770
Expect the first one very soon.

59
00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:29.274
Good-bye, Ebenezer, and good luck."

60
00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:34.338
Marley backed away, clanking his chains and moaning.

61
00:04:38.221 --> 00:04:41.224
Scrooge cowered as the ghost floated out through the window.

62
00:04:42.865 --> 00:04:45.728
After Marley was gone, Scrooge hurried to the window.

63
00:04:48.156 --> 00:04:53.661
Outside, the air was filled with phantoms floating here and there, moaning as they went.

64
00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.705
Every one of them wore chains like Marley's ghost.

65
00:05:00.006 --> 00:05:03.789
Scrooge went pale as he recognized some of his old business acquaintances.

66
00:05:06.611 --> 00:05:11.215
Turning away from the dreadful sight, he went to the door to make sure it was locked.

67
00:05:13.877 --> 00:05:17.600
Then, holding his head in his hands, he went into his bedroom.

68
00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:23.229
He climbed into bed and fell asleep instantly.

69
00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:28.191
Scrooge woke up some time later.

70
00:05:29.332 --> 00:05:31.993
It was very dark, and the church bell was ringing.

71
00:05:33.313 --> 00:05:38.055
Scrooge counted the bell's chimes, expecting them to stop, as they always did.

72
00:05:40.036 --> 00:05:42.377
But they continued on and on.

73
00:05:42.397 --> 00:05:46.459
"How strange," Scrooge thought.

74
00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.880
"Am I dreaming?"

75
00:05:50.108 --> 00:05:54.670
At last, the chimes stopped, and a loud bong shook the walls.

76
00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.252
At the same moment, an eerie light filled the room.

77
00:06:01.473 --> 00:06:05.854
Scrooge's eyes opened wide at the sight of a figure standing beside his bed.

78
00:06:07.135 --> 00:06:11.897
The figure was a strange combination of a young child and an old man.

79
00:06:13.237 --> 00:06:15.018
Its hair was long and white.

80
00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:19.520
But its face was smooth, without the slightest wrinkle.

81
00:06:21.008 --> 00:06:25.731
It wore a white tunic and held a fresh green holly branch in one hand.

82
00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:31.715
"I suppose you're one of the ghosts that Marley told me about?"

83
00:06:32.256 --> 00:06:34.397
Scrooge's voice shook as he spoke.

84
00:06:34.417 --> 00:06:36.839
"I am."

85
00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.761
The ghost's voice was soft and gentle.

86
00:06:40.781 --> 00:06:44.444
"Do you have a name?"

87
00:06:45.044 --> 00:06:46.125
Scrooge asked.

88
00:06:47.766 --> 00:06:50.488
"I am the Ghost of Christmas Past."

89
00:06:51.784 --> 00:06:54.688
The spirit clasped Scrooge gently by the arm.

90
00:06:58.492 --> 00:07:00.454
and walk with me."
